WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.283
- I'm after yours.

00:00:01.283 --> 00:00:03.213
- Oh my God! I'm after yours.

00:00:03.213 --> 00:00:05.208
We should tradesies after the show.

00:00:05.208 --> 00:00:06.420
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.100
- Well, I'm gonna start
with congratulations.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.074
New son, right?

00:00:09.074 --> 00:00:09.907
- Yes. Thank you very much.

00:00:09.907 --> 00:00:10.740
Yes. Six months old.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:11.573
- [Kelly] How? Six months?

00:00:11.573 --> 00:00:12.810
Oh, are you sleeping?

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:13.643
- More... Yeah.

00:00:13.643 --> 00:00:14.476
Like he's doing okay.

00:00:14.476 --> 00:00:15.850
He's sleeping more than we are.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:16.683
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.631
(all laugh)

00:00:17.631 --> 00:00:19.800
- So you have a two year old, right?

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:20.633
- [Lindsay] Yes.

00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:21.466
- So do you do Halloween?

00:00:21.466 --> 00:00:22.299
Do y'all get all done up?

00:00:22.299 --> 00:00:23.132
I love Halloween.

00:00:23.132 --> 00:00:25.217
- Well as someone who
dresses up for a living,

00:00:25.217 --> 00:00:27.600
it's not like my favorite
thing to put on a costume,

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.433
but of course, like,

00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:30.840
my daughter really
wanted us to do "Frozen."

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:31.681
- [Kelly] Yeah. Oh!

00:00:31.681 --> 00:00:36.330
- [Lindsay] So, she's Anna
and I am gonna be Elsa

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:39.090
and my partner's gonna be Kristoff.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.830
And so that's fun.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.350
She has no idea that Uncle
Jonathan is Kristoff.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.920
That'll be mind blowing when
she figures that out but...

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.097
- Oh my God. Yeah, she'd lose it.

00:00:48.097 --> 00:00:48.930
- [Lindsay] I know.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:49.763
- It is funny when...

00:00:49.763 --> 00:00:51.600
because my kids saw an
animated thing that I did

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.730
and they were like, it broke the wall.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:54.563
- [Lindsay] Oh God!

00:00:54.563 --> 00:00:55.950
- It was kind of intensely sad.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:56.863
- [Daniel] Oh no.

00:00:56.863 --> 00:00:57.696
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:57.696 --> 00:00:58.890
They saw me in this
movie called "Ugly Dolls"

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:00.420
and they were like, "We
don't understand," but like,

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.620
and I was like, "Well,
you know, like Elsa,

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.150
like, you know, like she's a real person,"

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:04.230
And they were like, "What?"

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.137
And I was like, "Oh my God!"

00:01:05.137 --> 00:01:05.970
- [Daniel] "Oh no.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.230
What have I ruined?"

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.360
- I felt like a horrible human.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:10.193
- Yeah.

00:01:10.193 --> 00:01:11.026
- [Kelly] But, you know,
it was gonna happen

00:01:11.026 --> 00:01:11.859
sooner or later.

00:01:11.859 --> 00:01:13.470
- I do that to kids on
like a regular basis

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.274
when they're like, "It's Harry,"

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:16.380
and I'm like, "I'm sorry."

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:17.739
They're like, "You're
old now. What happened?"

00:01:17.739 --> 00:01:20.683
(all laugh)

00:01:20.683 --> 00:01:21.516
- So that was what's so funny.

00:01:21.516 --> 00:01:23.130
My daughter was obsessed with Chris Martin

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.360
for, like, I mean years.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.800
And she always watched the "Yellow" video,

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:26.910
but he's younger.

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:27.900
It's his first single.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:28.860
And so whenever she saw him,

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:30.090
she's like, "Well, he looks different."

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.104
I go, "Well, we age, honey."

00:01:31.104 --> 00:01:32.246
But yeah.

00:01:32.246 --> 00:01:33.750
Okay. Enough about kids.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:34.740
So I have to get to this.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.810
I heard that you went to
Beyonce's Renaissance tour.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:38.580
Was it four times?

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:39.516
Four times.

00:01:39.516 --> 00:01:41.502
(audience cheers)

00:01:41.502 --> 00:01:42.990
- [Kelly] I have a question.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:44.160
I haven't been...

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.440
So, is it like "O" like you can keep going

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.580
and you see something new?

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.428
Like, you know the "O" in Vegas?

00:01:49.428 --> 00:01:50.730
- [Jonathan] Yes, yes.

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:52.710
I would say... I mean, I haven't seen "O."

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:53.543
- [Kelly] Oh, you can...

00:01:53.543 --> 00:01:55.092
I can go again and see something...

00:01:55.092 --> 00:01:55.925
- [Jonathan] You could, yeah.

00:01:55.925 --> 00:01:57.609
I'm sure it's amazing.

00:01:57.609 --> 00:01:58.442
- [Kelly] Look at you!

00:01:58.442 --> 00:01:59.977
- [Jonathan] That's me
at Beyonce with Jenny T.

00:01:59.977 --> 00:02:01.118
- [Kelly] You whipped your hair.

00:02:01.118 --> 00:02:02.674
- [Jonathan] Yes.

00:02:02.674 --> 00:02:03.507
That's me and Jenny T.

00:02:03.507 --> 00:02:04.740
- [Kelly] You look like Patrick Swayze

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.660
in "Dirty Dancing" right
now. What's happening?

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.204
- [Jonathan] You just made my life.

00:02:09.204 --> 00:02:10.037
(Lindsay and Daniel laugh)

00:02:10.037 --> 00:02:10.870
- [Kelly] That is really what you..

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:12.180
like, with your tank and you're sweaty

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.170
and the little curl.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.670
It was like nice. Okay, okay.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.253
- [Jonathan] I mean, he is God.

00:02:16.253 --> 00:02:17.117
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah.

00:02:17.117 --> 00:02:18.960
- Yeah. You really can go again and again.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.970
I've already got tickets of...

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.200
I've got them for these two.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.794
If they're joining me
or not, I don't know.

00:02:23.794 --> 00:02:24.627
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:02:24.627 --> 00:02:27.000
- On the 1st of December,
when the movie comes out,

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.478
the concert movie of Beyonce
is coming out. The film.

00:02:29.478 --> 00:02:30.311
- Oh my God!

00:02:30.311 --> 00:02:31.410
- For after our show that Friday night.

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:33.138
- I'm not doing anything after
the show. Are you insane?

00:02:33.138 --> 00:02:34.076
- I'm not either. We have children.

00:02:34.076 --> 00:02:35.340
- You might though. You might.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.073
I might get you to go.

00:02:37.073 --> 00:02:38.580
- [Kelly] I am so these people.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.350
I'm like, "I'm tired."

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:41.220
- [Daniel] For Beyonce?

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.322
- [Jonathan] Yes. But for
Beyonce it's different.

00:02:43.322 --> 00:02:45.338
And the concert...and I...

00:02:45.338 --> 00:02:47.670
It's transcendent.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:48.677
It's a transcendent experience.

00:02:48.677 --> 00:02:49.510
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:50.430
It's amazing to be in a concert like that.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:52.890
- Before we did this, we
do eight shows a week.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:55.290
It's a lot of the same show every night

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.520
of Merrily We Roll Along.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:57.353
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:57.353 --> 00:02:59.070
- And watching Beyonce,

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.450
all the four times that I saw it

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.280
all the times that I
watched her on YouTube

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.429
in all the other cities...

00:03:03.429 --> 00:03:04.463
- I love you so much.

00:03:04.463 --> 00:03:07.020
- [Jonathan] Like she
brought it to every city,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.120
no matter which country, which city.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.020
It was always new.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.879
She was always in a
different outfit and...

00:03:12.879 --> 00:03:13.712
- [Kelly] Oh, really?

00:03:13.712 --> 00:03:15.210
- [Jonathan] It inspired
me for the run of our show,

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.741
that every time you perform live,

00:03:16.741 --> 00:03:18.750
there's new people out there.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.580
You have to bring everything you've got.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.002
So it was a real source of inspiration.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.060
I'm clearly passionate.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.230
- You have a poster of her in your room.

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.063
- I have. Yes.

00:03:26.063 --> 00:03:28.170
Krystal Joy Brown, who
plays Gussie in our show.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.003
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:29.003 --> 00:03:30.930
- As a gift got me the Renaissance poster

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:32.610
and she's there in the dressing room.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:33.443
- She's there every day.

00:03:33.443 --> 00:03:34.276
- Part of the show.

00:03:34.276 --> 00:03:35.109
- I look at her every day.

00:03:35.109 --> 00:03:36.210
- So I had this experience with you too.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.530
I saw 'em at Madison Square Garden and

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.230
I left half wanting to quit music.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.490
But, the other half of
me was so inspired and

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.323
it is... It does...

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.220
It's like, man, they've been doing this

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.360
for so long and it's such,

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.520
it renews like a certain
passion inside you.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:48.390
- [Jonathan] Yes. Completely.

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:49.830
- [Kelly] Yeah. I love that for you.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.385
Have you ever seen
anybody that many times?

00:03:51.385 --> 00:03:52.218
- No.

00:03:52.218 --> 00:03:53.051
- [Lindsay] No.

00:03:53.051 --> 00:03:53.884
- [Kelly] No?

00:03:53.884 --> 00:03:54.717
- No.

00:03:54.717 --> 00:03:55.550
- [Kelly] Is there someone you would see?

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:57.060
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:58.620
Is there someone you think you would,

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:00.600
like, if you had the
time and no babies or...

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.510
- I mean, yeah, there's
definitely bands that like,

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:04.920
but I don't think anyone like,

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.140
the hold steady anyone.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:07.973
Nobody.

00:04:07.973 --> 00:04:08.806
(audience cheering)

00:04:08.806 --> 00:04:09.657
- [Kelly] Oh, you're like you...

00:04:09.657 --> 00:04:11.521
- So I'm like, yeah, there's definitely,

00:04:11.521 --> 00:04:12.480
I love trying new stiff...

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.000
but like there's
definitely people I would.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.980
But not...probably four times
is stretching it though?

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:17.813
Is there anyone you would say that much?

00:04:17.813 --> 00:04:18.646
- I don't know.

00:04:18.646 --> 00:04:19.740
Maybe like Barbra Streisand.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:21.480
- [Kelly] Like, oh, I've never seen her.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.313
- Me neither.

00:04:22.313 --> 00:04:23.250
I would die to see her.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:24.083
We should go...

00:04:24.083 --> 00:04:26.338
- If she comes to New
York, we are gonna go.

00:04:26.338 --> 00:04:27.171
- [Lindsay] Yep. We're gonna go.

00:04:27.171 --> 00:04:28.004
- [Kelly] You think I'm
kidding, but I'm not.

00:04:28.004 --> 00:04:30.050
- No. I'm serious. I'm like...

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.440
- [Kelly] I don't feel
like she does shows though.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:32.273
- I don't know.

00:04:32.273 --> 00:04:33.106
I'm just saying like,

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:33.939
if we put it out in the universe.

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:34.920
- [Kelly] Did you see the thing she did,

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.360
the music and Memories thing she did

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:37.380
at like Netflix or something?

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:38.310
It was some kind of thing.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.270
Oh my! I'm weeping.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.410
- [Jonathan] Yeah, she did it in Brooklyn.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:41.451
This concert.

00:04:41.451 --> 00:04:42.284
(Kelly gasps)

00:04:42.284 --> 00:04:43.117
- Yeah and...

00:04:43.117 --> 00:04:43.950
- And her new book's about to come out.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:44.783
- [Kelly] Oh really?

00:04:44.783 --> 00:04:45.616
- Yes.

00:04:45.616 --> 00:04:46.449
- [Kelly] I want her on the show.

00:04:46.449 --> 00:04:47.580
I was like, wait.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:48.870
I was like, we share a birthday.

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:49.703
I love you.

00:04:49.703 --> 00:04:51.070
(all laughing)

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:51.903
- [Kelly] Do I get any points there?

00:04:51.903 --> 00:04:53.370
- Wait, the song I picked for you

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.770
for your Spotify playlist,
is a Barbra song.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.150
It's an obscure Barbra song.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:58.620
- [Kelly] How obscure?

00:04:58.620 --> 00:04:59.453
What's it called?

00:04:59.453 --> 00:05:00.559
Oh, you're not gonna tell me.

00:05:00.559 --> 00:05:01.392
- It's called Napoleon.

00:05:01.392 --> 00:05:03.052
- [Kelly] Oh, I don't know that one.

00:05:03.052 --> 00:05:04.920
- [Kelly] I feel like there's a complex,

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.240
I feel like is this a fun song?

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.860
'cause you could go a lot
of ways with Napoleon.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:09.120
- [Jonathan] It's a very fun song.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.470
- [Kelly] Okay. Okay. Okay.

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:12.150
Did y'all know each other
before you got on stage?

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:13.950
'cause I feel like you,
even the voice coaches

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:14.940
they have us have like a dinner

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.200
or get together for drinks or something.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.160
If you've never met each other

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.840
and they have us kind
of you know, hang out.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:19.980
- That would've been nice.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:20.813
- Yeah.

00:05:20.813 --> 00:05:21.646
- [Kelly] Oh, you did...

00:05:21.646 --> 00:05:23.010
Was the first day just... Oh!

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:25.530
- No, we've known each
other for a long time.

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:26.363
- Yeah.

00:05:26.363 --> 00:05:28.440
- But you know, we knew
we were doing this for,

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:29.490
I don't know, a year or something.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:32.070
So we all... We got each other's info

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:34.620
and started sending video text messages

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.090
back and forth to get to know each other.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:37.440
- [Daniel] Which I was
slightly stressed out by,

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:38.400
because these guys send like,

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.850
very relaxed, natural
sort of 2-3 minute videos

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:42.960
giving an update.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:44.760
And I was always just watching them.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:45.990
And when I would try and send back,

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.490
I would have to restart
it like three times,

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:48.323
'cause I'm like, oh,

00:05:48.323 --> 00:05:49.590
I'm saying "um" an "ah too much.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:50.818
Or I'm saying (indistinct)

00:05:50.818 --> 00:05:51.651
(all laughing)

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:52.590
- And then they would...

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.000
I would feel like I had to make notes and

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.590
just like, what everything did they say

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:56.550
in their videos that I...

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:57.510
- [Kelly] Oh my god!

00:05:57.510 --> 00:05:59.580
- [Daniel] I have become
more relaxed about it

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:00.660
since then. Thank God.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.620
- [Kelly] Good for you.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:02.648
- Yeah. It's real growth.

00:06:02.648 --> 00:06:03.481
Thank you.

00:06:03.481 --> 00:06:05.048
(all laughing)

00:06:05.048 --> 00:06:05.881
- [Jonathan] You've great video.

00:06:05.881 --> 00:06:07.234
- [Daniel] I do now. Thank you.

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:08.067
- [Jonathan] Great video.

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:08.900
- [Kelly] Well he worked on them.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:09.733
They should be pretty good.

00:06:09.733 --> 00:06:10.566
(all laughing)

00:06:10.566 --> 00:06:11.936
- I've been. Yeah. Rehearsing apparently.

00:06:11.936 --> 00:06:12.769
(audience cheering)

00:06:12.769 --> 00:06:13.920
- I recently moved here.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:16.043
I love working here. Thank you.

00:06:16.043 --> 00:06:17.580
But what do y'all like about working here?

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:18.413
Do you like it?

00:06:18.413 --> 00:06:19.260
Do you like living here and working here?

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:20.970
- Oh, I mean, anytime I
get to work in New York

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:22.080
it's kind of the dream.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.610
Like I live here most of the time.

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.140
I mean, pretty much.

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:26.100
Yeah. I live here now, basically.

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.390
I think I can say that.

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:29.700
And yeah, anytime I get to also work here

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:30.533
and just like come home

00:06:30.533 --> 00:06:32.490
to my place at the end of the day

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:34.260
and be in the, you know West Village.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.490
It's awesome. I love this city.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.291
So, I feel really lucky
to be able to live here.

00:06:37.291 --> 00:06:38.124
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:38.124 --> 00:06:39.780
And raising kids here is kind of fun!

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:40.620
- It's amazing!

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:41.760
- [Kelly] I didn't
think that would happen.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:42.593
- [Lindsay] There's much for them here.

00:06:42.593 --> 00:06:43.426
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:43.426 --> 00:06:45.030
- [Lindsay] 'cause I was
living in LA too for a while

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:47.100
and came back here for this and Oh my God!

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:50.370
Like the parks and the museums
and taking her, you know

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:52.830
on the bus and on the
subway, like, it's so fun.

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.260
We just, we have such a
full life here with kids.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.190
It's fantastic.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.480
- [Kelly] Yeah. Do you love it?

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:58.380
- Obsessed. I love it.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:06:59.375
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:06:59.375 --> 00:07:00.208
- Yeah.

00:07:00.208 --> 00:07:01.041
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:07:01.041 --> 00:07:01.874
- [Jonathan] I put on my bike helmet.

00:07:01.874 --> 00:07:02.707
I get on my bicycle.

00:07:02.707 --> 00:07:03.540
- [Kelly] You're one
of those brave people.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:04.373
- [Lindsay] Yeah.

00:07:04.373 --> 00:07:05.206
- [Kelly] I haven't done that yet.

00:07:05.206 --> 00:07:06.039
- [Jonathan] It's so...

00:07:06.039 --> 00:07:08.070
I recommend maybe in Central Park first

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.144
before you move to the streets.

00:07:09.144 --> 00:07:10.110
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.730
I have a bike coming and I just...

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:13.560
I also see the ER in my future.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:14.490
I just, I don't know.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:15.323
- [Jonathan] Yeah, yeah yeah.

00:07:15.323 --> 00:07:16.156
- [Kelly] I just feel like,

00:07:16.156 --> 00:07:17.430
people can drive crazy here little bit.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:18.263
- [Lindsay] Yes.

00:07:18.263 --> 00:07:19.096
- [Daniel] Yeah.

00:07:19.096 --> 00:07:20.190
- [Jonathan] Yeah. It's
intense in those bike lanes.

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:21.101
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:21.101 --> 00:07:22.680
- But it's also beautiful and incredible

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:24.450
and riding the bike to the theater.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:26.700
My favorite thing about New
York is the live theater,

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:29.475
that like eight times a week,
there's all of these people

00:07:29.475 --> 00:07:34.080
in this like, small area of New
York performing these plays.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:35.640
It's such a special place.

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.590
- [Kelly] That's an amazing
way to look at it too.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:40.380
Yeah. And just, it's
not gonna last forever.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:41.220
That show's gonna leave...

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:42.480
So it's like, you wanna catch it like,

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:44.160
the energy of that is pretty magical.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:44.993
- Exactly.

00:07:44.993 --> 00:07:45.826
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:45.826 --> 00:07:46.659
Well explain to everybody

00:07:46.659 --> 00:07:47.910
if that doesn't know
Merrily We Roll Along.

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:48.783
What is it about?

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:50.820
Who wants time go?

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:51.760
- [Jonathan] Am I taking this one?

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:53.160
- [Daniel] Jonathan's got this one.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.723
- You were all like, "Not me."

00:07:54.723 --> 00:07:55.556
- [Lindsay] Yes.

00:07:55.556 --> 00:07:57.510
- [Jonathan] So, Merrily We Roll Along,

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:59.550
is a story of three friends,

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:02.880
a friendship that spans 20 years,

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.470
but it's a musical.

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:06.330
Music and lyrics by Stephen Sondheim,

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:08.370
incredible composer of Into the Woods

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:10.050
and Sunday in the Park with George.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:12.870
And the unique thing, or
one of the unique things

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:15.900
about the show is that it's
about a 20 year friendship,

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:17.730
but it's told backwards.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.950
So it starts at the end of the friendship

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:21.180
and goes all the way back

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:23.640
to the beginning when they first met.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.440
- [Kelly] And the music is amazing.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:26.487
Sondheim is amazing.

00:08:26.487 --> 00:08:28.830
(all laughing)

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:30.210
- [Kelly] So, I know I haven't seen it.

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:32.040
My executive producers like, get to this.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.540
I'm just, my kids' just got in school

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:34.410
and there's all these parent-teacher.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.790
Gosh. So I haven't been able to catch yet.

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:36.623
- [Daniel] Don't worry.
It's fine. It's cool.

00:08:36.623 --> 00:08:37.456
Don't worry. Thank you.

00:08:37.456 --> 00:08:38.289
- [Kelly] I know. But
there's so many shows.

00:08:38.289 --> 00:08:39.900
I have a list with my
girlfriends for our night...

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:40.823
We have one night at a week.

00:08:40.823 --> 00:08:42.297
- [Daniel] When you come
let us know. No pressure.

00:08:42.297 --> 00:08:43.620
- [Kelly] No. I'm not gonna let you know,

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:44.880
because you're like me.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:45.713
- [Daniel] Oh yeah.

00:08:45.713 --> 00:08:46.860
- You don't like to know when people come.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:47.693
- Let us know.

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:48.526
- [Kelly] I don't either.

00:08:48.526 --> 00:08:49.680
- They won't tell me. I'll find out later.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:50.513
Then, that's fine.

00:08:50.513 --> 00:08:51.496
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:08:51.496 --> 00:08:52.329
- [Kelly] Okay. We are identical in this.

00:08:52.329 --> 00:08:53.850
'cause I don't like when people tell me

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:54.990
people are at my show because I will,

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:55.950
one, think about it the whole time

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:56.970
and then I will search for them.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:57.803
- [Daniel] Yes.

00:08:57.803 --> 00:08:58.636
- [Jonathan and Lindsay] Oh!

00:08:58.636 --> 00:08:59.815
- I was told recently,

00:08:59.815 --> 00:09:01.050
there was a moment like,

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:03.480
three weeks ago where Meryl Streep

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.017
was supposed to be coming
to the show for the night.

00:09:05.017 --> 00:09:06.510
- [Kelly] You never tell someone,

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:08.340
Meryl Streep is coming.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:09.207
- Right.

00:09:09.207 --> 00:09:12.780
And I accidentally found
out and then I was like,

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:13.613
she didn't end up coming.

00:09:13.613 --> 00:09:14.717
I think she had something else to do.

00:09:14.717 --> 00:09:15.550
- Oh my gosh!

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:16.383
- [Daniel] She's a busy woman.

00:09:16.383 --> 00:09:18.540
But like, I for the whole time..

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:19.373
'cause that's the thing

00:09:19.373 --> 00:09:20.790
when if I know that like an anonymous

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.340
famous person is in the
crowd, I'm fine with it.

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:25.380
As soon as I know specifically who it is

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:27.570
I keep thinking like, "Oh God, you know,

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:28.950
Robert De Niro is out there thinking...

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:29.783
watching my acting tonight."

00:09:29.783 --> 00:09:30.690
That's a terrifying thought.

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:33.030
But he is a psychopath.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:33.863
- Yeah.

00:09:33.863 --> 00:09:34.696
- And he likes knowing.

00:09:34.696 --> 00:09:35.529
- He loves to know.

00:09:35.529 --> 00:09:36.362
- You're opposite.

00:09:36.362 --> 00:09:37.195
- [Jonathan] I love to know.

00:09:37.195 --> 00:09:38.028
- Yep.

00:09:38.028 --> 00:09:38.861
- I love to know.

00:09:38.861 --> 00:09:40.710
When I was doing Hamilton with Lin,

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:43.230
we shared a dressing room
and I used to be like,

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:44.760
I don't know if I like to know or not

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:47.040
but Lin obsessively wanted to know

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:48.120
who was in the audience

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:52.080
and it would bring him so much joy

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:54.570
and it would infuse
his performance with...

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:55.459
- [Kelly] Well, he used it.

00:09:55.459 --> 00:09:56.292
- [Jonathan] He used it.

00:09:56.292 --> 00:09:57.125
So like when Eminem was there,

00:09:57.125 --> 00:09:58.800
who's like one of his rap heroes,

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:02.760
he was like rapping in
a slightly harder way.

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:04.440
When Meryl was there,

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:05.790
we were all giving like,

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.590
very acted performances of Hamilton.

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:09.772
- [Kelly] Sophie's choice level.

00:10:09.772 --> 00:10:11.460
- [Jonathan] Yes. It was very...

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:13.680
We were like suddenly
conscious of everything

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:15.031
that we were doing with our hands.

00:10:15.031 --> 00:10:16.440
(all laughing)

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:17.970
- [Jonathan] That's like
the vibe I feel when...

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.127
- [Kelly] I'm completely him. No.

00:10:19.127 --> 00:10:20.962
- [Jonathan] You are
like, you as well. Right.

00:10:20.962 --> 00:10:21.795
- [Kelly] Do you like to know?

00:10:21.795 --> 00:10:22.628
- I'm kind of in the middle.

00:10:22.628 --> 00:10:25.920
Like if I find out, I
mean, and the truth is like

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:28.860
at Merrily we've had so
many people come now..

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:29.693
- [Kelly] Well that's good.

00:10:29.693 --> 00:10:30.846
Then it becomes normal.

00:10:30.846 --> 00:10:31.679
- [Lindsay] It kind of has
started to become normal.

00:10:31.679 --> 00:10:33.247
But I used to be like him and be like,

00:10:33.247 --> 00:10:34.800
"Don't tell me" or I'll be the entire

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.360
show thinking how bad I am.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.193
- [Daniel] Yeah. We all
thought Tom Hanks was there

00:10:37.193 --> 00:10:38.400
the other day. He was not.

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:39.233
- I know.

00:10:39.233 --> 00:10:40.066
- We've had it confirmed.

00:10:40.066 --> 00:10:40.899
It was not him.

00:10:40.899 --> 00:10:41.732
There's a guy who looks a lot like him

00:10:41.732 --> 00:10:42.570
who seeing shows in New York.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:43.720
- [Kelly] Doppelganger.

